---
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { company, email } from '../../site';

const subject = encodeURIComponent('Delete my Wallyt account');
const body = encodeURIComponent(
  'Please delete my Wallyt account. I am sending this from the email address I sign in with.',
);
---

<Doc
  title="Delete your Wallyt account"
  eyebrow="Wallyt"
  meta={`Wallyt, by ${company.brand}`}
  section="wallyt"
  description="How to delete your Wallyt account, what is deleted, and what stays with your groups."
>
  <p>
    You can ask us to delete your Wallyt account and the personal data that goes with it at any
    time. You don’t need the app installed to do it.
  </p>

  <h2>How to delete your account</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${email.privacy}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`}>{email.privacy}</a> from the email address you use to sign in to Wallyt, with the subject “Delete my Wallyt
      account”.
    </li>
    <li>
      We reply to confirm. If you write from a different address, we’ll send a code to your Wallyt
      address to check the account is yours.
    </li>
    <li>We delete your account within 30 days, and email you when it’s done.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>If you own a group</strong> that has other people in it, you can make someone else the
      owner first, from the group’s settings. Otherwise we pass ownership to one of its admins, or to
      another member if it has none.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What we delete</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account: your email address, name and photo.</li>
    <li>Your Google or Apple sign-in link, and every signed-in session.</li>
    <li>Your email address and photo from each group you were in.</li>
    <li>Groups where you were the only person, with all their expenses and history.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays with your groups</h2>
  <p>
    Expenses are shared records: the other people in a group rely on them for their own balances.
    So expenses and payments you were part of, and their history, stay in those groups. They
    show the name you had in that group, but nothing else about you, and they’re no longer
    connected to an account. The other people in the group can still edit or delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>
  <p>
    Your account is deleted within 30 days of your request. If any copy of it remains in a backup,
    it is erased within 30 days after that.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting some data without closing your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Remove or change your photo and name in Wallyt, from Account.</li>
    <li>Leave a group from its settings. Its past expenses keep your name, as described above.</li>
    <li>
      To have something else removed, such as a photo someone added of you or an expense, email <a href={`mailto:${email.privacy}`}>{email.privacy}</a> and tell us what it is.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Read the full <a href="/wallyt/privacy">Wallyt privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>
